            "description": "NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5 controls implemented by custodian.",
            "implemented-requirements": [
              {
                "control-id": "au-10",
                "description": "Each message is MLS-signed by its sender, and the sender's copy is sealed to the custodian's ML-KEM-1024 key with its hash bound into the signed data and the log entry. Opening the archive needs a DS-logged ReadArchive permit for a listed records officer. Hybrid: the procedure is enforced by the custodian binary, not by cryptography, so the key holder can bypass it (Q16), and a sender can seal a copy that differs from what members got (Q17).",
                "links": [
